# There is no published paper or archival DOI yet; the manuscript is in
# preparation and anonymized for review. Update the author list, add
# `doi:` and `preferred-citation:` when the preprint is posted, and keep
# the Citation section of README.md in step.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ariadne, please cite the repository until the paper appears."
title: "Ariadne: federated question answering over live cybersecurity knowledge graphs"
abstract: >-
  Ariadne answers security-analyst questions across live cybersecurity knowledge
  graphs that do not share a query language, routing each sub-question natively
  per engine (Cypher to Neo4j, Gremlin to a Neptune-style server), reconciling
  results on shared identifiers rather than a shared index, and returning claims
  that each cite the record and the executed query behind them.
type: software
authors:
